From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:00:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 014/154] atrium: native window corner radius; concentric
 nested radii
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The window corner was too square against Safari and Finder. The probe that
reads the native radius built a toolbar-LESS NSWindow, and the value is
style-dependent: stock NSThemeFrame caches 16 for a plain titled window but 26
once the window carries a toolbar, which is the class Atrium is in. Give the
probe a toolbar and it reports the right value, still read back from AppKit
rather than hardcoded.

Measured, not guessed - shadowless `screencapture -o` captures expose the
silhouette's real alpha edge, where the earlier screenshot attempt drowned in
the drop shadow's falloff. Corner extent @2x: Safari 63px, Finder 63px,
TextEdit and Ghostty (no toolbar) 35px. Atrium now measures 63px on all four
corners. Confirmed independently by an AppKit probe across style masks
(toolbar -> 26.00, no toolbar -> 16.00), and end-to-end against the running
app via ATRIUM_WINDOW_CORNER_RADIUS: 20 -> 50px, 26 -> 63px, 32 -> 81px.

Moving the window radius exposed the second bug: every nested radius was a
hardcoded literal tuned against the old value, so they silently desynced. Fix
the cause rather than the numbers - derive them concentrically (inner = outer
- gap) so the curves stay parallel and the gap reads uniform around the
corner instead of pinching at 45 degrees. Content card 12 -> 16, floating
sidebar overlay 12 -> 21 (rounder: it sits a smaller step in from the edge).

- atrium_corner_radius.{h,cc}: the pure rule, own source_set + gtest
  (capture_math's posture), floored at 6 so deep insets cannot read square.
- atrium_window_corner_radius.{h,mm}: the AppKit probe, lifted out of
  atrium_browser_window.mm's anonymous namespace so the sidebar overlay's
  translation unit can reach it. ATRIUM_WINDOW_CORNER_RADIUS still overrides.
- Collapses ~4.3KB of superseded comments documenting two theories
  that the measurements disproved.

Verified: 8/8 new gtests, full atrium filter green, chrome builds clean, and
the card gap measures 10.0pt along both straight edges and 9.7-9.9pt through
the diagonal - a non-concentric card looks right on the edges and pinches only
at the corner, so measuring one edge would have proved nothing.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
